 "result": "I fixed the bug in `calc/pricing.py`, and `test_discount_rounding` now passes.\n\n`apply_discount` was cutting off the extra decimals with `int()` instead of rounding. In floating point, 2.30 \u00c3\u2014 0.5 \u00c3\u2014 100 comes out as 114.999\u00e2\u20ac\u00a6, so `int()` turned it into 114 and the function returned 1.14 instead of 1.15. I changed line 7 to round to the nearest cent:\n\n```python\nreturn round(price * (1 - pct / 100) * 100) / 100\n```\n\nI didn't touch the test.",
